---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Crumbs from '../../../components/Crumbs.astro';
import ReviewNote from '../../../components/ReviewNote.astro';
import GiftEstimateDesk from '../../../components/GiftEstimateDesk.astro';
import {url, SITE} from '../../../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Gift estimate desk" description="Map one deliberately selected gift to an exact reproduced source model, inspect the assumptions and save or requalify one conditional estimate. Unlinked gifts remain unknown.">
  <header class="page-head"><div class="wrap"><Crumbs items={[{label:'Tools',href:'/tools/'},{label:'Giving Dashboard',href:'/tools/giving-dashboard/'},{label:'Gift estimate desk'}]} /><p class="eyebrow">Page-only tool · authored hypothesis</p><h1>Inspect the link<br />between a gift and a model.</h1><p class="lede">A dollar amount or depth description cannot tell you what a gift achieved. Make one source link explicit, test the calculation and keep its limits beside the result.</p></div></header>
  <div class="wrap estimate-body">
    <div class="prose"><h2>A conditional case, with unknowns visible</h2><p>Charitology studies the signals, channels, work, outcomes and feedback around giving. This desk helps inspect one proposed link in that system. It does not measure delivery or donor causation, judge a charity or treat depth as effectiveness. Relief, repair, prevention, structure and source describe different mechanisms; every level may be needed.</p><p>One selected gift can produce a <strong>conditional modeled estimate with authored assumptions</strong>. Other gifts and the unmapped portion remain unknown. Sample gifts and illustrative sources stay hypothetical. There is no lifetime impact total or combination of outcomes in this first method.</p><p>Start with the <a href={url('/tools/giving-dashboard/')}>Giving Dashboard’s native JSON export</a> and one <a href={url('/tools/cost-effectiveness-model-kit/')}>Model Kit selected-version export</a>. A compatible source needs a referenced artifact checksum, nominal USD in the gift year, an exact program period and a positive lower cost stated as exact plain-decimal cents. Unsupported or missing information stays unknown.</p></div>
    <GiftEstimateDesk />
    <section class="prose"><h2>What the range means</h2><p>The fixed source simulation supplies cost-per-outcome draws. This method applies your mapped amount and fixed donor-credit fraction to each draw, then calculates new percentiles. The p5–p95 range describes those entered model assumptions. It is not a confidence interval or a probability that the gift worked. Uncertainty in applicability, additionality, fungibility, credit and omitted harms is not modeled.</p><p>Fresh numerical reproduction checks software consistency. Your source description, checksum, applicability and allocation remain authored claims. They do not establish scientific review, source rights, marginal funding or actual impact. This desk neither endorses nor rates a named organization.</p><p><a href={`${SITE.repo}/blob/main/src/lib/gift-estimate/arithmetic-v1.mjs`}>Read the complete adjacent arithmetic method</a> · <a href={`${SITE.repo}/tree/main/src/lib/gift-estimate`}>Inspect the open consumer and file contracts</a> · <a href={url('/method/')}>Read Charitology’s Method</a></p></section>
    <ReviewNote filePath="src/lib/gift-estimate" title="Gift estimate desk" />
  </div>
</Base>
<style>.estimate-body{padding-bottom:3rem;min-width:0}.estimate-body>.prose{margin:2rem 0;max-width:75ch}</style>
